  #line-at(352.573pt, 234.245pt, "3. SURROGATE MODEL FOR SPM ")
  #line-at(304.815pt, 251.765pt, "Physics-based battery models typically involve partial ")
  #line-at(304.805pt, 263.289pt, "differential equations (PDEs), which significantly slow down ")
  #line-at(304.805pt, 274.693pt, "numerical simulation. To enable real-time implementation, we ")
  #line-at(304.795pt, 286.216pt, "employ the concept of PINN to solve the PDEs embedded in ")
  #line-at(304.795pt, 297.74pt, "the SPM, resulting in a surrogate model referred to as the ")
  #line-at(304.795pt, 309.264pt, "physics-informed SPM (PI-SPM). In this section, we provide ")
  #line-at(304.785pt, 320.788pt, "a concise introduction to PINNs, describe the network ")
  #line-at(304.785pt, 332.192pt, "architectures that can be employed, and discuss how ")
  #line-at(304.785pt, 343.716pt, "nondimensionalization ")
  #line-at(407.627pt, 343.716pt, "and ")
  #line-at(433.55pt, 343.716pt, "hard ")
  #line-at(463.074pt, 343.716pt, "constraints ")
  #line-at(517.916pt, 343.716pt, "can ")
  #line-at(543.355pt, 343.716pt, "be ")
  #line-at(304.785pt, 355.239pt, "incorporated to facilitate more efficient training. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(304.785pt, 374.801pt, "3.1 Physics-informed neural network ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(304.775pt, 392.201pt, "PINNs constitute a class of deep learning models that embed ")
  #line-at(304.775pt, 403.725pt, "the governing physical laws, typically expressed as PDEs, ")
  #line-at(304.775pt, 415.248pt, "directly into the training objective. Consider a general time-")
  #line-at(304.775pt, 426.892pt, "dependent PDE defined in a spatiotemporal domain ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(535.777pt, 426.892pt, "Ω ⊂")
  #line-at(304.775pt, 439.013pt, "ℝ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(312.24pt, 435.24pt, "𝑑𝑑")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(319.56pt, 438.96pt, "× [0, 𝑇𝑇]")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(351.342pt, 438.96pt, ": ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(374.021pt, 458.641pt, "𝒩𝒩[𝑢𝑢(𝑥𝑥, 𝑡𝑡)] = 0, (𝑥𝑥, 𝑡𝑡) ∈Ω,")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(304.799pt, 478.202pt, "subject to the initial and boundary conditions ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(317.399pt, 497.883pt, "𝑢𝑢(𝑥𝑥, 0) = ℎ(𝑥𝑥),")
  #line-at(401.272pt, 497.883pt, "𝑢𝑢(𝑥𝑥, 𝑡𝑡) = 𝑔𝑔(𝑥𝑥, 𝑡𝑡),")
  #line-at(492.376pt, 497.883pt, "(𝑥𝑥, 𝑡𝑡) ∈∂Ω.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(304.829pt, 517.564pt, "Here, ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(330.387pt, 517.564pt, "𝑥𝑥")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(337.11pt, 517.564pt, " and ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(357.747pt, 517.564pt, "𝑡𝑡")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(363.025pt, 517.564pt, " denote the spatial and temporal coordinates, ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(304.829pt, 529.208pt, "𝒩𝒩")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(317.787pt, 529.208pt, "is a general linear or nonlinear differential operator, ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(304.829pt, 540.97pt, "𝑢𝑢(𝑥𝑥, 𝑡𝑡)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(332.598pt, 540.97pt, " represents the PDE solution, ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(460.464pt, 540.97pt, "ℎ(𝑥𝑥)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(480.075pt, 540.97pt, " is the prescribed ")
  #line-at(304.819pt, 552.733pt, "initial condition, and ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(389.659pt, 552.733pt, "𝑔𝑔(𝑥𝑥, 𝑡𝑡)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(417.746pt, 552.733pt, "defines the boundary condition on ")
  #line-at(304.829pt, 564.496pt, "the boundary ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(363.513pt, 564.496pt, "𝜕𝜕𝜕𝜕")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(377.318pt, 564.496pt, ". This formulation is general and can be ")
  #line-at(304.839pt, 576.02pt, "readily extended to higher-order PDEs by rewriting them as ")
  #line-at(304.829pt, 587.543pt, "systems of first-order equations. ")
  #line-at(304.829pt, 607.224pt, "To approximate the unknown solution ")
