  #line-at(123.24pt, 255pt, "𝑑𝑑")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(128.4pt, 252.96pt, " are weighting coefficients balancing the ")
  #line-at(42.605pt, 264.603pt, "different loss components. Minimizing ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(211.686pt, 264.603pt, "ℒ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(219.843pt, 264.603pt, " ensures that the ")
  #line-at(42.605pt, 276.246pt, "learned solution satisfies both observational data and ")
  #line-at(42.605pt, 287.77pt, "governing physics. PINNs have demonstrated strong potential ")
  #line-at(42.605pt, 299.294pt, "in solving forward and inverse problems, parameter estimation, ")
  #line-at(42.605pt, 310.818pt, "and uncertainty quantification. Their ability to unify data-")
  #line-at(42.605pt, 322.222pt, "driven learning with physical constraints makes them a ")
  #line-at(42.605pt, 333.746pt, "powerful ")
  #line-at(90.004pt, 333.746pt, "tool ")
  #line-at(116.644pt, 333.746pt, "for ")
  #line-at(139.564pt, 333.746pt, "scientific ")
  #line-at(187.204pt, 333.746pt, "machine ")
  #line-at(232.325pt, 333.746pt, "learning ")
  #line-at(276.244pt, 333.746pt, "and ")
  #line-at(42.605pt, 345.269pt, "computational modeling. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(42.605pt, 364.831pt, "3.2 Model architecture ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(42.605pt, 382.231pt, "As illustrated in Fig. 2, three different model architectures are ")
  #line-at(42.605pt, 393.755pt, "constructed: a split architecture, a merged architecture, and a ")
  #line-at(42.605pt, 405.278pt, "DeepONet-based architecture. The first two architectures are ")
  #line-at(42.605pt, 416.802pt, "based on conventional PINN structures, while the third ")
  #line-at(42.615pt, 428.326pt, "corresponds to the PI-DeepONet model. All three architectures ")
  #line-at(42.605pt, 439.73pt, "have the same inputs: time, space, and current. In the split ")
  #line-at(42.615pt, 451.254pt, "architecture, the two concentration states are predicted ")
  #line-at(42.615pt, 462.777pt, "independently using two separate neural networks. The ")
  #line-at(42.615pt, 474.301pt, "advantage of this configuration is that the network parameters ")
  #line-at(42.615pt, 485.825pt, "are not shared, allowing each network to better capture the ")
  #line-at(42.615pt, 497.348pt, "specific characteristics of its corresponding state. In contrast, ")
  #line-at(42.615pt, 508.753pt, "the merged architecture employs a single neural network to ")
  #line-at(42.615pt, 520.276pt, "predict both concentrations simultaneously. Since the two ")
  #line-at(42.615pt, 531.8pt, "states satisfy similar governing equations, sharing parameters ")
  #line-at(42.615pt, 543.324pt, "enables ")
  #line-at(83.78pt, 543.324pt, "a ")
  #line-at(99.383pt, 543.324pt, "more ")
  #line-at(131.185pt, 543.324pt, "compact ")
  #line-at(176.19pt, 543.324pt, "architecture ")
  #line-at(234.641pt, 543.324pt, "and ")
  #line-at(260.323pt, 543.324pt, "reduces ")
  #line-at(42.615pt, 554.848pt, "computational complexity. The third architecture is based on ")
  #line-at(42.605pt, 566.371pt, "DeepONet, where the modification is introduced by adding a ")
  #line-at(42.605pt, 577.775pt, "linear layer (the blue block in Fig. 2) after combining the ")
  #line-at(42.605pt, 589.299pt, "outputs of the branch and trunk networks, enabling the ")
  #line-at(42.605pt, 600.823pt, "prediction of both states. Because DeepONet is designed to ")
  #line-at(42.605pt, 612.347pt, "learn mappings between input and output functions (i.e., ")
  #line-at(42.605pt, 623.87pt, "operators), it is expected to provide superior performance ")
  #line-at(42.605pt, 635.394pt, "when handling dynamic current inputs. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(101.28pt, 755.76pt, "Figure 2. Architecture of the PI-SPM.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(304.8pt, 80.283pt, "3.3 Nondimensionalization ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(304.8pt, 97.68pt, "Data normalization is an important preprocessing step in ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 109.204pt, "machine learning, which involves transferring the input ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 120.727pt, "features and output into a similar scale, and can make the ")
  #line-at(304.81pt, 132.251pt, "training process more stable and converge faster. In the SPM, ")
  #line-at(304.81pt, 143.775pt, "there is one microscopic coordinate (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(472.218pt, 143.775pt, "r")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(476.062pt, 143.775pt, ") and a temporal ")
  #line-at(304.82pt, 155.299pt, "coordinate (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(352.459pt, 155.299pt, "t")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(355.217pt, 155.299pt, "). These multi-scale features often make the PINN ")
  #line-at(304.83pt, 166.703pt, "training fail to converge (Wang et al., 2022). Similar to the ")
  #line-at(304.82pt, 178.227pt, "data/features ")
  #line-at(367.827pt, 178.227pt, "normalization, ")
  #line-at(437.667pt, 178.227pt, "the ")
  #line-at(461.789pt, 178.227pt, "nondimensionalization ")
  #line-at(304.83pt, 189.75pt, "technique in PINN has been proven to have a significant ")
  #line-at(304.83pt, 201.274pt, "impact on model accuracy and convergence speed (Wang et ")
  #line-at(304.83pt, 212.798pt, "al., 2023). In the nondimensionalization process of SPM, the ")
  #line-at(304.84pt, 224.322pt, "coordinates ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
