  #line-at(310.44pt, 288.6pt, "Figure 4. Performance of the PI-SPM (DeepONet) model under the ")
  #line-at(316.083pt, 298.923pt, "test conditions. (a) Boundary-condition (BC) loss and PDE loss. ")
  #line-at(316.083pt, 309.246pt, "(b) Terminal voltage. (c) Positive-electrode surface concentration. ")
  #line-at(316.083pt, 319.803pt, "(d) Negative-electrode surface concentration. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(304.8pt, 340.92pt, "Furthermore, we evaluated the model performance under ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 352.444pt, "current conditions beyond the upper boundary of the training ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 363.967pt, "data (10 A) to test the model’s extrapolation capability, where ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 375.491pt, "the test currents of 11 A and 13 A were selected. The results ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 386.895pt, "indicate that the extrapolation performance of the split and ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 398.419pt, "merged architectures shows no significant difference. Both ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 409.943pt, "models produce accurate predictions at 11 A but exhibit ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 421.466pt, "noticeable degradation at 13 A. These observations suggest ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 432.99pt, "that the models possess a certain degree of extrapolation ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 444.514pt, "capability, but only within a limited range. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(310.44pt, 575.52pt, "Figure 5. Model performance under extrapolation conditions (left: ")
  #line-at(316.083pt, 585.96pt, "11 A, right: 13 A). ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(304.8pt, 607.2pt, "4.2 PI-SPM under dynamic current condition ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(304.8pt, 624.6pt, "In real applications, discharge currents can vary arbitrarily, ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 636.124pt, "and it is impossible to cover all possible current profiles in the ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 647.648pt, "training data. As a result, learning the relationship between ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 659.171pt, "highly dynamic current inputs and the resulting concentration ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 670.575pt, "distributions becomes particularly challenging for neural-")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 682.099pt, "network-based surrogate models. To simplify the task, we first ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 693.623pt, "consider a low-frequency dynamic current profile generated ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 705.147pt, "using Gaussian Random Fields (GRF), with the current ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 716.67pt, "magnitude ranging from 1 to 10 A. ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 736.112pt, "Fig. 6 illustrates the training results of three architectures ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 747.636pt, "under only one dynamic current in the train dataset. Among ")
  #line-at(304.8pt, 759.16pt, "the three models, only the DeepONet-based PI-SPM performs ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 5.253pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
