#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-06.png", width: 496pt), 50.5pt, 78pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(48.24pt, 259.2pt, "Figure 9. Model performance under high-frequency current ")
  #line-at(53.892pt, 269.523pt, "conditions. (a) A sample of the RSC profile. (b) Surface ")
  #line-at(53.892pt, 279.846pt, "concentrations without Fourier feature mapping. (c) Surface ")
  #line-at(53.883pt, 290.403pt, "concentrations with Fourier feature mapping. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(42.6pt, 311.52pt, "4.3 Model evaluation on labeled data ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(42.6pt, 329.04pt, "In the previous section, when trained without labeled data, the ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 340.563pt, "split and merged PI-SPM models failed to learn the correct ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 352.087pt, "mapping between the GRF current input and the concentration ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 363.491pt, "distribution. The central idea of physics-informed modeling is ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 375.015pt, "to combine data information with physical constraints to ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 386.539pt, "achieve both accurate and generalizable predictions. However, ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 398.062pt, "studies in the existing literature often rely exclusively on either ")
  #line-at(42.6pt, 409.586pt, "the physics-based loss or the data-based loss, and few have ")
  #line-at(42.59pt, 421.11pt, "investigated how incorporating labeled data can improve ")
  #line-at(42.59pt, 432.514pt, "model performance. In this section, we examine the influence ")
  #line-at(42.59pt, 444.038pt, "of labeled data on training performance, focusing on the ")
  #line-at(42.59pt, 455.561pt, "merged PI-SPM architecture. ")
  #line-at(42.59pt, 475.123pt, "During training, a specified number of labeled samples are ")
  #line-at(42.59pt, 486.527pt, "randomly selected from the reference dataset in each batch and ")
  #line-at(42.59pt, 498.051pt, "incorporated into the loss function as the data loss term. We ")
  #line-at(42.58pt, 509.574pt, "evaluate the merged PI-SPM under different numbers of ")
  #line-at(42.58pt, 521.098pt, "training current profiles and different numbers of labeled ")
  #line-at(42.58pt, 532.622pt, "samples. The results are shown in Fig. 10. ")
  #line-at(42.58pt, 552.064pt, "The observations reveal several important trends. First, even a ")
  #line-at(42.58pt, 563.588pt, "single labeled sample is sufficient to guide the neural network ")
  #line-at(42.58pt, 575.111pt, "toward the correct solution. Increasing the number of labeled ")
  #line-at(42.58pt, 586.635pt, "samples beyond approximately ten does not yield further ")
  #line-at(42.58pt, 598.039pt, "accuracy improvements, indicating diminishing returns. ")
  #line-at(42.58pt, 609.563pt, "Second, the merged PI-SPM achieves very low error when ")
  #line-at(42.57pt, 621.087pt, "trained on a single current profile. However, when trained on ")
  #line-at(42.57pt, 632.61pt, "two current profiles, its error increases substantially, and the ")
  #line-at(42.57pt, 644.134pt, "degradation is even more pronounced when trained on three ")
  #line-at(42.57pt, 655.658pt, "profiles. Compared with the DeepONet-based PI-SPM in Fig. ")
  #line-at(42.56pt, 667.062pt, "8, this highlights a fundamental limitation of conventional ")
  #line-at(42.56pt, 678.586pt, "PINN-based architectures: while they can achieve high ")
  #line-at(42.55pt, 690.109pt, "accuracy for a single PDE with fixed boundary conditions, ")
  #line-at(42.55pt, 701.633pt, "they struggle to learn a family of PDEs with varying boundary ")
  #line-at(42.55pt, 713.157pt, "conditions—demonstrating ")
  #line-at(171.795pt, 713.157pt, "weaker ")
  #line-at(221.12pt, 713.157pt, "operator-learning ")
  #line-at(42.55pt, 724.681pt, "capability than DeepONet. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(310.44pt, 265.8pt, "Figure 10. Training results of the merged PI-SPM with different ")
  #line-at(316.083pt, 276.24pt, "numbers of labeled samples. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(388.8pt, 297.48pt, "5. CONCLUSIONS ")
  #line-at(304.797pt, 314.88pt, "This work systematically evaluates three physics-informed ")
  #line-at(304.797pt, 326.404pt, "surrogate architectures for the SPM, namely split PI-SPM, ")
  #line-at(304.787pt, 337.928pt, "merged PI-SPM, and DeepONet-based PI-SPM. Under ")
  #line-at(304.777pt, 349.451pt, "constant-current conditions, all models achieve good accuracy ")
  #line-at(304.767pt, 360.975pt, "and proper extrapolation capability. However, when dynamic ")
  #line-at(304.767pt, 372.499pt, "current profiles are introduced, fundamental differences ")
  #line-at(304.767pt, 383.903pt, "emerge. ")
  #line-at(348.935pt, 383.903pt, "The ")
  #line-at(376.539pt, 383.903pt, "conventional ")
  #line-at(440.124pt, 383.903pt, "PINN-based ")
  #line-at(501.684pt, 383.903pt, "architectures ")
  #line-at(304.757pt, 395.427pt, "consistently fail to learn PDE solutions under dynamic ")
  #line-at(304.757pt, 406.95pt, "boundary ")
  #line-at(354.08pt, 406.95pt, "conditions ")
  #line-at(407.245pt, 406.95pt, "without ")
  #line-at(449.248pt, 406.95pt, "labeled ")
  #line-at(489.572pt, 406.95pt, "data, ")
  #line-at(520.176pt, 406.95pt, "whereas ")
  #line-at(304.757pt, 418.474pt, "DeepONet-based PI-SPM remains effective but requires ")
  #line-at(304.757pt, 429.998pt, "hundreds of training current samples to generalize properly. ")
  #line-at(304.757pt, 441.521pt, "For highly dynamic inputs such as Random Step Currents, ")
  #line-at(304.757pt, 452.926pt, "DeepONet exhibits spectral-bias limitations and struggles to ")
  #line-at(304.747pt, 464.449pt, "capture high-frequency concentration dynamics. Incorporating ")
  #line-at(304.747pt, 475.973pt, "spatio-temporal Fourier feature mappings significantly ")
  #line-at(304.747pt, 487.497pt, "mitigates this issue, enabling accurate prediction of fast ")
  #line-at(304.747pt, 499.021pt, "transients. To demonstrate the data efficiency, we also ")
  #line-at(304.747pt, 510.425pt, "investigate how different amounts of labeled data influence ")
  #line-at(304.757pt, 521.948pt, "model accuracy. ")
  #line-at(304.757pt, 539.468pt, "Overall, this study clarifies the operating regimes under which ")
  #line-at(304.757pt, 550.992pt, "PINN-based SPM surrogates remain feasible and identifies ")
  #line-at(304.747pt, 562.516pt, "Fourier-enhanced DeepONet as a more robust approach for ")
  #line-at(304.747pt, 574.039pt, "realistic, highly dynamic battery-operation scenarios. These ")
  #line-at(304.737pt, 585.443pt, "insights provide a practical foundation for developing more ")
  #line-at(304.747pt, 596.967pt, "generalizable physics-informed surrogate models for battery-")
  #line-at(304.747pt, 608.491pt, "management applications. ")
  #line-at(304.747pt, 626.01pt, "Several important questions remain open for future research. ")
  #line-at(304.747pt, 637.654pt, "The SPM is applicable only at low C-rates (")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(507.304pt, 637.654pt, "≤")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(514.744pt, 637.654pt, "1C), and ")
  #line-at(304.747pt, 649.177pt, "constructing surrogate models for the P2D or even multi-")
  #line-at(304.747pt, 660.701pt, "physics frameworks with strong generalization remains highly ")
  #line-at(304.747pt, 672.225pt, "challenging. Physics-encoded models (Faroughi et al., 2024; ")
  #line-at(304.728pt, 683.749pt, "Huang et al., 2024) may offer promising directions in this ")
  #line-at(304.728pt, 695.272pt, "regard. Furthermore, model parameters may vary as functions ")
  #line-at(304.728pt, 706.796pt, "of temperature, stress, and aging. How to enable surrogate ")
  #line-at(304.728pt, 718.2pt, "models to capture parameter variability is another important ")
  #line-at(304.728pt, 729.724pt, "challenge. Although some studies (Brendel et al., 2025; ")
  #line-at(304.738pt, 741.248pt, "Hassanaly et al., 2024b; Panahi et al., 2025) have included ")
  #line-at(304.738pt, 752.771pt, "selected parameters as neural-network inputs, physics-based ")
  #line-at(304.737pt, 764.295pt, "battery models typically contain more than twenty parameters, ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 5.765pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(173.345pt, 150.648pt, "(a)")
  #line-at(114.641pt, 237.77pt, "(b)")
  #line-at(227.889pt, 237.77pt, "(c)")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 5.41pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(324.335pt, 78.614pt, "Random sampling in every batch ")
]

